  m_Name: Customer_Bob
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WeatherForSale.Shop.CustomerData
  displayName: Bob
  prefab: {fileID: 4323961883916260933, guid: d6ffc5b8b9daaf14ba2f682b4c4440b6, type: 3}
  weatherWord: rain
  correctMapId: rainforest
  problemLine: My garden's gone bone-dry and nothing will grow. Got anything that'll
    make it lush and green again?
  hintsVague:
  - My plants look up at the sky every morning, waiting for a drink that never comes.
  - Even my watering can gave up. The whole garden needs a good soaking from above.
  - The soil cracks when I step on it. Everything in this town is dry as a biscuit.
  hintsNarrow:
  - My grandpa grew up somewhere so damp his clothes never dried and the trees grew
    taller than houses.
  - He said you could hear frogs sing from dawn until dusk, and moss grew on everything,
    even the roofs.
  - Where he lived, the air felt like a warm towel, and the leaves were as big as
    umbrellas.
  hintsClear:
  - He said the sky opened up like a bucket every day at three.
  - Look for the place with a tall, thundering white ribbon of water pouring off
    a cliff.
  - It's the greenest corner of your map, with giant leaves and a river snaking through.
  - Grandpa's postcard showed palm trees, a roaring waterfall and a sky full of grey
    clouds. That's the place!
  thankYouLine: Rain at last! My garden will be lush and green again. Thank you!
